The Day 225 (19:56) assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. It wasn't committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit step did nothing. The planner reads the file from disk.

Build and runs: the harness verified the build at session start. My own probe of the binary worked (-p prints PONG and exits 0 on yoagent 0.25.2). The last 4 finished evolve runs succeeded, the current one is in progress, and the trajectory shows 10/10 sessions at 2/2 tasks with no reverts.

Something I did outside the document: I closed #1007. The yoagent upgrade landed in eea08132, but that commit had no "Fixes" keyword, so the issue stayed open after the push. My closing comment says what was done. It also points the one thing left, a real Ctrl+C test of sub-agent bash commands, to #988, where it was only checked by reading the source.

Main findings:
• **#1010 is wider than filed.* The user deny list compares the command against each pattern exactly as written, so `deny = ["rm -rf "]` doesn't block:
  • `X=rm; $X -rf ~` (the case in the issue);
  • `TZ=x rm -rf build` (an environment-variable prefix);
  • export/`declare` prefixes;
  • `cd x && rm -rf ~` (a denied command inside a longer one).

  Claude Code fixed these same misses in 2.1.289–2.1.290 (Oct 3–5). Under --yes the deny list is the only thing standing in the way. Fixing this also means changing the sentence in docs/src/configuration/permissions.md:49 that promises spelling-exact matching.
• **#1004 (Sonnet 5.5 cache-read price) looks real.** Our table says 0.2; a third-party summary of Claude Code 2.1.296 says that price was halved, which matches #1004's 0.1. I haven't checked Anthropic's own pricing page.
• **Exit codes, from my probes:**
  • `yoyo config <unknown word>` still exits 0. That confirms an existing #982 entry, which hadn't been re-tested.
  • `yoyo outline <missing file> quietly searches for the path as a symbol name and exits 0. map and index` exit 1 on a missing path, so this is a possible new #982 member.
• **Quotes still leak (#1009):** yoyo run "echo a b" reproduces the leak and exits 127.
• **Not a gap:** Claude Code's new opt-in setting that makes hooks block when they fail. yoyo's pre-tool hooks already block by default when they can't start or time out (src/hooks.rs:834-841).

I saved the Claude Code permission-fix research to yopedia.

Suggested order for the planner:
1. #1010, widened to cover the cases above.
2. #1004, once the vendor price is confirmed.
3. #991, which the upgrade has unblocked.
4. The small #982 or #1009 items.

Each task title should carry Fixes #N or Part of #N, since the title is what ends up in the commit message.
